```
  Detection : Brute force followed by a successful logon
  MITRE     : T1110 Brute Force (T1110.001 Password Guessing, T1110.003 Password Spraying)
  Data      : Windows Security Event Log (4625 failed logon, 4624 successful logon)
  Logic     : A source IP with >= 10 failures AND >= 1 success in the search window
  Severity  : High (Critical if the source is external and Logon_Type = 10 / RDP)
  Author    : Ifeanyi Solomon Uneze
```
index=wineventlog (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4624) Logon_Type IN (3, 10)
| eval outcome=if(EventCode=4624, "success", "failure")
| stats count(eval(outcome="failure")) AS failures
        count(eval(outcome="success")) AS successes
        dc(TargetUserName)             AS distinct_accounts
        values(TargetUserName)         AS accounts
        values(host)                   AS targets
        min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        BY IpAddress
| where failures >= 10 AND successes >= 1
| eval attack_type=if(distinct_accounts > 5, "Password spraying", "Password guessing")
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - failures

```
  TUNING
  - Exclude vulnerability scanners: add  NOT IpAddress IN ("10.0.0.50")  to the first line
  - Exclude service accounts with known expired-password noise
  - Lower the threshold for privileged accounts (e.g. admin*, svc_*)
```
